<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Privacy manifest for CallerAPILiveCallerID.

      The Live Caller ID Lookup query itself is run by iOS (Oblivious HTTP +
      Privacy Pass + keyword PIR), which hides the looked-up number from the
      CallerAPI backend - that path collects nothing.

      Separately, the optional metering/version-check heartbeat (Metering.swift,
      host app only) collects a Device ID (identifierForVendor) to count active
      devices per app for billing and to report the SDK version. It is NOT used
      for tracking (no linking across apps/developers, no advertising), so
      NSPrivacyTracking remains false. If your app does not call
      configureMetering(...), no Device ID is collected - remove the Device ID
      entry below in that case.

      Device attestation (AppAttest.swift) uses Apple's App Attest to prove the
      request comes from a genuine, unmodified build of this app. The key is
      generated in the Secure Enclave and never leaves it; nothing about the
      device or the user is collected, and DeviceCheck is not a required-reason
      API, so no additional declaration is needed for it.

      Required-reason APIs: UserDefaults, used to read/write the App Group
      container that shares the per-user tier token between the host app and the
      extension, to cache the metering fallback id, and to remember this app's own
      App Attest key identifier. All are this app's own data, so reason CA92.1.
    -->
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeDeviceID</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
            <true/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
            <false/>
            <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
            <array>
                <string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
